        <rule description="Sedimentary rock composed of at least 30 percent rounded to subangular fragments larger than 2 mm in diameter; typically contains finer grained material in interstices between larger fragments. If more than 15 percent of the fine grained matrix is of indeterminant clastic or diagenetic origin and the fabric is matrix supported, may also be categorized as wackestone. If rock has unsorted or poorly sorted texture with a wide range of particle sizes, may also be categorized as diamictite." filter="representativeLithology_uri = 'http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/generic_conglomerate' OR representativeLithology_uri = 'http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/genericConglomerate'" key="{829bdd9f-5579-499e-8bef-0a57f489be05}" label="generic conglomerate" symbol="116"></rule>
